etic with marco  and what he's trying to do  so i think there's real potential there  that they might split up or something  might happen  to undermine drummer's authority in  going against marco  trying to collect the bounty at the same  time it doesn't seem likely that she  would join up with the free navy  unless she does so under the pretenses  of having a plan to  take him out that way based on what  we've seen he has a far superior  fleet it's not clear that she knew this  before and so it's likely that when she  finds out  she'll have to figure out a plan if she  still wants to go after him  marco is in a pretty strong position  right now the coordinated nature of his  attack  has everyone back on their heels and his  using the proto-molecule as  a threat makes it more complicated for  anybody from the inner planets trying to  go after him the thing with him using  the gemara code is that he was never  caught for the original  attack naomi wrote it in a way that it's  mostly  undetectable in the book whenever naomi  makes the call to jim they'd already  been running system checks to see if  anything had been wrong with it  so even though we didn't see them do  that in the show it's very possible that  they did  and they weren't able to find it using  something like that is just another  example of where people have to fear him  they have to take him seriously  the gemara code makes the ship's  magnetic bottle fail  and that more or less turns the reactor  into a nuclear bomb  the ship becomes a nuclear bomb that was  why it was so crazy to see  sakai double down when she was locked in  the cell  she knew the ship was going to blow up  it was going to take a big part of the  station with it and it was probably  going to take her out as well  that's the kind of threat that makes all  the stations feel  unsafe and now belters are going to have  to decide if they're going to fall in  line behind the free navy or not  sin did a great job of laying out the  belter 